  "body": "Hello,\r\nwe use VOIP calls functionality in riot.im mobile client\r\nWe've found strange behavior , when user changes network on his mobile device \r\nFor example:\r\n1) User 1 calls User 2 (WIFI connected phone) (Audio call) -> they speak -> they close conversation\r\n2) User 2 switches out of WIFI network to 3G network\r\nUser 1 calls User 2 (3G connected phone) (Audio call) -> they try to speak, but User 1 can't hear User 2. \r\n3) User 2 closes riot.im app -> opens it again -> User 1 calls User 2 (3G connected phone) (Audio call) -> they speak. Everyone can hear each other\r\n\r\nSeems like there is something like timeout at which client device updates its IP address.\r\nMaybe thi is riot.im mobile client prblem =(",
